Corrected message:

Make edge strokes undoable in eraser, pencil, recolor and freeform

These tools decided whether a stroke changed anything from whether the
pointer was inside the canvas. A wide stroke dragged along an edge, or
a fast drag sampled off opposite edges, painted the canvas with the
pointer outside it and left no undo step. Each tool now checks whether
the area it actually painted overlaps the canvas, as the paintbrush
already did; the paintbrush now shares the same helper.

Adds a regression test and updates the changelog entry.
